sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant H as Host service (@Transactional)
  participant RE as RuleEngine (core)
  participant C as Compiled cache (replica)
  participant DB as PostgreSQL (rle_*)

  H->>RE: evaluate("card-fee", input)
  RE->>RE: resolve tenant from host security context, clock from Clock bean
  RE->>C: get (tenant, card-fee)
  alt cache hit
    C-->>RE: published versions with effective_from, compiled trees
  else cache miss
    RE->>DB: SELECT published versions (tenant, rule set)
    RE->>RE: compile to typed tree, bind slots
    RE->>C: put, LRU bounded by cache.max-entries
  end
  RE->>RE: pick latest effective_from <= clock, bind inputs to slots, walk tree (no I/O)
  alt decision-log.mode = transactional
    RE->>DB: INSERT rle_decision (caller's connection and transaction)
  else decision-log.mode = async
    RE->>DB: INSERT rle_decision_outbox (caller's transaction, small row)
  end
  RE-->>H: DecisionResult (decisionId, version, outputs, matchedRuleIds)
  alt host commits
    H->>DB: COMMIT: business rows and decision row persist together
  else host rolls back
    H->>DB: ROLLBACK: no decision row, no orphan
  end
  Note over RE,DB: Errors (UNIQUE_HIT_VIOLATION, EVALUATION_ERROR) return no partial outputs and are logged with their outcome
